        "submission": "update.json",
        "summary": "No new evidence or change this cycle within the turn's remaining time; the draft bytes stand as previously accepted rather than a duplicate revision. The record is complete and consistent: one asserted defect with two independently witnessed producing conditions of the same mechanism (shouldSnapshot's unsigned delta underflow - a store-emptied node after a TrailingLogs=0 snapshot, CheckRun 9cba2e79ff6c4019b0f0381690d9aaab, and a follower whose log store sits below a snapshot it just installed, CheckRun e5116cfe896549deb27799d6d871ed77 - each scheduling a redundant snapshot at the unchanged index with no safety effect); three refuted suspicions with retained operands (non-voter commit eligibility; post-restart vote duplication, which also confirmed the durable last vote; the AddVoter configuration lag as a bounded replication transient, with the user-restore and non-quiescent install routes also measured not to produce the snapshot condition); and four durable Behaviors/Facts, including the voter-only commit set and the two snapshot-trigger facts. The only unmeasured aspect left is the actual cadence of the repeated snapshot attempts, which depends on the FSM continuing to answer Snapshot."
